2.1 The reflexive move
Treatments of subjectivity typically append conditions to a model of cognition — temporal unification, self-modeling, valence — as new primitives. The conditions could as easily have been two, or six, or different ones.
They are not new primitives. They are the Part 1 capacities aimed at the system itself.
