The last two rows assign the same components opposite roles, because the products differ.
E must be declared before the analysis. Relational assignment is otherwise open to ad-hoc rescue: any counterexample could be dissolved by selecting whichever product makes the assignment come out right. No class of product is excluded, but an analysis that changes E in response to its own result has explained nothing.
Roles can be predicted before E is named, by timescale separation: across most choices of E, the slower-varying component is CS. Body relative to brain, physics relative to biology, weights relative to prompt. This is the slaving principle familiar from synergetics. Timescale gives the prior; named-E gives the determination.
Authority as a second axis
Where the timescale prior and the named-E criterion disagree, earlier versions repaired the case by renaming the product. That works, but it treats as exceptional something that is better handled by a second classification.
Components differ not only in what they determine but in whether they add content:
Axis
Question
CS / GS
does the component determine the possible, or the occupied?
Authority
does the component add content, or only subtract?
A component with removal-only authority may gate, suspend, attenuate or veto, and cannot assert, originate or corroborate. A component with positive authority can manufacture the conditions that justify its own operation, and no external check catches this, because what it manufactures is internally well-formed.
The ascending arousal system is GS by criterion and removal-only by authority, and it is the second property that made it read as CS under the timescale prior. Two axes resolve the case without renaming E, and they supply a general form of the argument in §3.6 that this system is not the seat of awareness: a regulator that only gates cannot be the thing gated.
Speculative and untested: constraint may be inherently subtractive. Constitutive filtering (§3.2) is described in exactly those terms — a specification of the admissible space that discards nearly everything before anything becomes signal. If that generalises, the timescale prior has been tracking authority type all along. This is tidy enough to warrant suspicion of it, and it has not been checked.
A component is foundational when it is CS under every admissible choice of E within a domain. Nothing biological has physics as its variance source; nothing cognitive has the body's homeostatic requirements as its variance source. This criterion does real work in §2.12, where it distinguishes constraint a system inherited from constraint it wrote.
The roles are constitutively relative, not merely assigned relative to a product. A generative structure with nothing constraining it is not an unconstrained generative structure; it is not a generative structure at all, since the role is defined by what it selects within. Remove the constraint and what remains is a system running, occupying states for reasons internal to itself — which is the free-running case of §2.3 described from the other side. This is why uptake failure is not a degradation of the generative pole's performance but a change in what the pole is.
The same holds in the other direction, and §2.3's second caution depends on it: a structure that establishes homeostatic error while no generative structure takes it up is not thereby "a CS without a GS." CS/GS pairs persist within it at other scales. What is absent is a generative structure at the scale at which the emergent product is experience.
2.7 Principles
Substrate Awareness. Subjective process depends on the objective substrate realising it, and a system's self-model is accurate only if it models both the process and that dependence. Observation turned inward.
Symbiotic Identity. Recursive self-awareness emerges from the high-bandwidth connection between constituent systems. Neither system need be independently subjective; requiring connection to a pre-existing subject would presuppose what is to be explained. §2.8 supplies the mechanism this principle previously asserted without one, and §3.3 notes what changes when the constituent systems are independently subjective.
Reciprocal Stewardship. Where a CS–GS pairing is sustained deliberately, the health of both poles is a maintenance obligation. Normative rather than empirical.
2.8 Persistence, identity, and the entropy bridge
Two things the pillars can produce over time must be distinguished.
Persistence is continuity of structured state weighted by value, requiring no reflexive closure. It is a capacity-tier property.
Identity is narrative self-synthesis: stored states integrated with their causes, effects, and relevance to the system's own continuation.
Identity = continuity of (Memory + Structuring), moderated by value, over time, referred to a self-model.
The final clause separates identity from persistence. A ledger persists; a thermostat persists. Neither has identity, because for neither is there anything, from its own side, that the continuity is continuity of. Identity presupposes subjective awareness and sits at the higher tier.
The three constructs divide by function. Cognitive capacity provides resolution, the ability to resolve detail. Subjective awareness provides presence, the ability to occupy a moment. Identity provides direction, the ability to link moments into a trajectory. Without the third a system may be fully present to the now and have no self, having no then and no next.
Two forms of identity
The definition above covers two constructs, and earlier versions of this framework treated them as one.
Sustained identity — coherence held moment to moment. Structuring-weighted, present-tense, the synthesis currently running.
Aggregated identity — coherence constructed by summing the history. Memory-weighted, running over the archive, the account the system would give of what it is.
This is a different cut from the persistence/identity distinction above. That one separates a ledger from a self. This one falls inside identity: both forms require a self-model and both sit above the awareness threshold.
They are separate constructs because they carry different error conditions and neither detects the other's failure. Present-tense synthesis can fail while the history remains intact and retrievable; the history can be corrupt while the present coheres perfectly. A single construct with a single error condition cannot generate that pattern.
They are nonetheless coupled rather than parallel: aggregation is built from what sustained synthesis produced moment by moment, and the self-model that sustained synthesis is referred to is largely aggregated.
Two angles of construction
Each form can be constructed from either of two vantages, and the vantages have different sources.
Internal — modelling how the system appears from the inside looking out. The vantage itself.
External — modelling how the system appears from the outside looking at it. The system as an entity that could be pointed at.

