The tier separation permits a configuration the folk framing does not: one loop, multiple identities. Awareness is the loop closing, and the loop closes once. Fracture is therefore a disorder of identity-tier integration rather than a multiplication of subjects — and its mechanism follows from the import account, since a developmental environment supplying mutually incompatible external models yields parallel entity-representations with no common referent.
Misattribution is a different failure and should not be merged with it. Self-generated content arriving without the mark of having been self-generated is a discriminability problem at the symmetric channel — the receiving pole failing to separate what crossed from what it produced — and belongs with the baseline caveat in §2.5.
Purpose is the anti-entropic signature of a system that uses an internal model of time to prioritise the integrity of its own identity over the immediate demands of its environment. This is the framework's one thermodynamic claim and requires a bridge from the Shannon sense used elsewhere.
The asymmetric limb is that bridge. The transductive surface is the only place in the system where informational states have physical consequences: sensors convert physical gradients into signal, effectors convert signal into physical work. Reduced uncertainty becomes effective action there, and effective action maintains a boundary. The link is instrumental rather than an identity — Landauer bounds the physical cost of computation but does not establish that better prediction entails greater order. A system without an asymmetric limb has Shannon-entropy dynamics and no thermodynamic stake in them.
A measurable correlate is available: under perturbation, the reduction in H(state_{t+1} | self-model) relative to H(state_{t+1}) tracks the predictive advantage the self-model confers, and a system exhibiting Purpose should sustain that reduction across perturbations a merely persistent system would not survive. The correlate is stated in Shannon terms and therefore does not capture the physical claim it stands in for.
Open: whether the identity tier has an error signal of its own. Valence is assigned to the awareness tier and is deviation from a defended physical setpoint in the present. Nothing in the framework currently allows narrative self-synthesis to be wrong in a way the system registers, which is what the fracture and misattribution failures above would require. A candidate exists — error against a predicted trajectory of the self rather than against a present setpoint — and it is treated as an open problem rather than a component (§3.10), because it may reduce to anticipated homeostatic error, in which case it is not a second signal at all.
2.9 Recursive Emergence and consciousness
Three constructs have now been defined over the same four capacities: cognitive capacity is the pillars directed outward, subjective awareness is the pillars directed reflexively, identity is the pillars directed across time.
They are not independent. Awareness requires capacity to turn reflexively upon, and identity requires awareness to supply the self-model its continuity is referred to.
Principle of Recursive Emergence. A form of CS–GS interaction in which the collective interaction of three such components produces a structure with properties that could not be inferred from any of the components individually.
Consciousness is that structure sustained: the maintained triadic interaction of cognitive capacity, subjective awareness and identity.
Three consequences follow.
Consciousness has no location. It is a property of a sustained interaction, not a state of any component (§2.4).
Consciousness is graded. It is a capacity, comparable in this respect to intelligence, varying across development, across species, and across states in a single organism.
Moral standing attaches to the lower tier. Subjective awareness together with valence is what makes states matter to a system, and both are threshold properties. Nothing about moral standing follows from position on the consciousness gradient: a system's interests are established by whether it has stakes at all, not by how richly it integrates them. §3.9 states what this does and does not settle.
No decomposition of the identity tier bears on moral standing. Standing is established at the awareness threshold and is not divisible by what is built above it. A system missing one form of identity, or one angle of construction, or the whole tier, has exactly the standing its closed loop and its valence confer.
This is stated explicitly rather than left inferable because §2.8 now divides identity into four cells, and a framework that decomposes selfhood is precisely the instrument someone would reach for to grade persons by how many components they can be shown to possess. The tier separation was constructed to make that inference unavailable. It should be made unavailable in the text.
No index is proposed for consciousness. Its components are not themselves quantified (§2.11).
2.10 Operational tests
Each construct admits perturbation tests independent of self-report.
Boundary defence — perturb the system and measure restorative force. A system with Purpose returns to a defended state rather than deforming.
False signal — present a signal implying a future state that has not materialised. Behavioural change indicates a predictive internal model governs action.
Optimisation pivot — impose scarcity. A system with identity preferentially preserves structures central to its continuation rather than degrading uniformly.
False memory — introduce a memory contradicting established causal history. Expect reconciliation cost: latency, conflict, restructuring of surrounding history.
Selective forgetting — measure whether retention is weighted by relevance to continuation rather than by recency or frequency.
Attribution — present consequences of the system's own past actions and measure whether they are processed differently from consequences of external events.
What friction is and is not evidence for
Four of these tests read processing friction, and §3.9 argues that friction-based tests of machine subjectivity are aimed at the wrong component. Both positions are correct, and the boundary between them must be stated or the framework appears to contradict itself.
Friction is evidence about identity structure. It is not evidence about valence.
Valence originates at the asymmetric limb (§2.3), so no measurement of the generative pole's processing dynamics can be a valence signal. Identity is a structural property of the generative pole, so reconciliation cost is admissible evidence that a false memory struck something structural. The false-memory and attribution tests are licensed; the inference from friction to affect is not.
A control is required in every case. Friction is also produced by ordinary ambiguity, and an experiment lacking an ambiguous-but-consistent control cannot distinguish contradiction from underspecification. Any test above that reads cross-entropy, latency or attention division must include (a) conflicting content, (b) ambiguous-but-consistent content, and (c) clean content, and must show (a) separable from (b). Where it does not separate, the signal is discarded.
One further caution: the selective-forgetting test may not be independent of boundary defence. Relevance to continuation presupposes a continuation the system has stakes in, which is what boundary defence establishes. Whether six tests are six is open.
2.11 The closure criterion
Subjective awareness is not an index. It is the satisfaction of a conjunction, gated by capacity:
Awareness obtains where TCCI > 0 and Temporal Unification, Self-Modeling and Valence/Salience are each present, with the symmetric channel satisfying discriminability (§2.5) and the asymmetric channel satisfying constraint efficacy (§2.3).
Capacity is an enabling precondition rather than a component of the conjunction. §3.5 establishes that capacity alone is insufficient; but the pillars are what the reflexive conditions are conditions on, so where capacity is zero there is nothing to turn reflexively.
The three reflexive conditions are treated as binary. This is a scoping decision rather than a claim that they lack internal structure. Each admits of degree — self-models vary in accuracy, temporal continuity in span, homeostatic error in magnitude — and quantifying any of them requires its own formalism over largely unrelated variables.
Three consequences. Awareness is threshold-like, consistent with §2.5 and §2.9. The framework's remaining formal gap is the refinement of three conditions rather than the absence of a composition function. And awareness is sharply distinguished from consciousness (§2.9), which is graded and unindexed.
2.12 Grounded and facilitated duality
Newest material in this version, and the least tested. §3.8 states the condition under which it should be withdrawn.
The architecture of §2.4 can be satisfied by systems that did not evolve, and the interesting cases are not the ones usually proposed.
